.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Euler showed in 1735 that \sum 1/n^2 = \pi^2/6, and in 1737 that the same sum is a product over the primes, \zeta(s) = \prod_p (1 - p^{-s})^{-1}. This script compares how fast the partial sums and the truncated Euler product approach \pi^2/6, and shows the product diverging at s = 1.">

